add("sun","The Sun",["sun","our star","sol","the sun"],
 "The Sun is our star: about 1,392,700 km across (109 Earths wide) and 333,000 times Earth's mass. Its surface is about 5,500 °C and its core about 15 million °C. It's about 4.6 billion years old, and its light takes about 8 minutes 20 seconds to reach Earth.",
 "NASA Sun Fact Sheet (NSSDCA) and NASA Science: Sun","solar","body:Sun",
 {"size":"The Sun is about 1,392,700 km across, 109 times Earth's width; about 1.3 million Earths would fit inside.","temp":"The Sun's visible surface is about 5,500 °C (5,772 K); the core is about 15 million °C.","dist":"The Sun is 1 AU from Earth: about 149.6 million km, or 8 minutes 20 seconds at light speed.","age":"The Sun is about 4.6 billion years old, roughly halfway through its life.","mass":"The Sun has about 333,000 times Earth's mass and holds 99.8% of the Solar System's mass."})
