add("2mrs","2MASS Redshift Survey (2MRS)",["2mrs","2mass","2mass redshift survey","blue dots"],"2MRS (Huchra et al. 2012) measured redshifts of the brightest infrared galaxies over almost the whole sky. It's the nearby, all-sky layer of this map: 43,105 galaxies out to about 1 billion light-years (about 300 Mpc).","Huchra et al. 2012, ApJS 199, 26","survey","home")
add("sdss","Sloan Digital Sky Survey (SDSS)",["sdss","sloan","sloan digital sky survey","sdss dr17","white dots"],"SDSS has mapped the sky with a 2.5 m telescope in New Mexico since 2000. This map uses 183,012 galaxies from its DR17 main galaxy sample (z 0.01 to 0.09). SDSS data revealed the Sloan Great Wall.","Abdurro'uf et al. 2022, ApJS 259, 35 (SDSS DR17)","survey","home")
add("desi","DESI",["desi","dark energy spectroscopic instrument","desi dr1"],"DESI uses 5,000 robotic fibre 'fingers' on the 4 m Mayall telescope in Arizona to measure millions of redshifts. This map uses 497,614 galaxies from DESI Data Release 1 (bright galaxies, luminous red galaxies and emission-line galaxies), reaching back about 9.6 billion years.","DESI Collaboration 2025, DR1 (arXiv:2503.14745)","survey","home")
add("surveys","Galaxy surveys on this map",["survey","surveys","where does the data come from","data","is it real","is this real","real data","source"],"Every dot is a real galaxy measured by a survey: 2MRS (the whole sky, nearby), SDSS DR17, and DESI DR1 (deep). Their positions come from redshifts. The alien is a cartoon; the galaxies are real.","Huchra et al. 2012; SDSS DR17; DESI DR1","survey","home")
